language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ set_game: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Set is a card game. The deck has 81 cards, each with a number of shapes (one, two or three), a shape (diamond, squiggle or oval), a shading (solid, striped or open) and a colour (red, green or purple). Three cards form a set when, for each of the four features, the three cards show that feature either all the same or all different. Given a list of cards, each written as [number, shading, color, shape], find three different cards that form a set.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `set_game.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/set_game.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `set_game_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py set_game.json
$   savilerow model.eprime set_game_1.param -run-solver

$ number of cards on the table, derived from the data: the length of cards_data (not a field of the reader's JSON)
given cards_data_dim1 : int
letting ncards = cards_data_dim1
$ cards_data[c, f]: feature f of card c, indices 1-based (the data's index 0 is cards_data[1, 1]); feature 1 is the number, 2 the shading, 3 the colour, 4 the shape, each as a code of that feature
given cards_data : matrix indexed by [int(1..ncards), int(1..4)] of int

$ winning_cards[k]: 0-based index of the k-th card of the set, so cards_data row winning_cards[k] + 1
find winning_cards : matrix indexed by [int(1..3)] of int(0..ncards-1)

such that
$ the three cards are different cards
allDiff(winning_cards),
$ for each of the four features, the three cards show that feature either all the same or all different
forAll f : int(1..4) .
  ((cards_data[winning_cards[1] + 1, f] = cards_data[winning_cards[2] + 1, f] /\
    cards_data[winning_cards[2] + 1, f] = cards_data[winning_cards[3] + 1, f]) \/
   allDiff([cards_data[winning_cards[1] + 1, f], cards_data[winning_cards[2] + 1, f], cards_data[winning_cards[3] + 1, f]]))
